# Workflow
1. Open `plan.md` and pick the next incomplete items that fit ~200-300 lines of work.
2. Sync `main` locally (`git checkout main` + `git pull`).
3. Create a feature branch from `main`.
4. Implement the selected `plan.md` items in code and docs.
5. Update `plan.md` checkboxes locally (do not commit `plan.md`).
6. Verify changes with `git status` and ensure only intended files are staged.
7. Commit changes with a clear message.
8. Push the branch to origin.
9. Create a PR from the branch.
10. Watch PR checks until they complete.
11. Merge the PR and delete the branch.
12. Pull `main` again and continue with the next `plan.md` items.

## Notes
- Keep each PR focused on a single roadmap chunk (~200-300 lines).
- If checks fail, fix on the same branch and re-run checks.
- Avoid staging `plan.md` (it is tracked only locally).
- Update docs and tests when new flags or behavior are added.
- Capture PR URL and check status in notes.
- Switch back to `main` after merging.
- Continue only after checks pass.
